ients with ischaemic stroke or TIA</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>2006</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>577</fpage><lpage>617</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16432246</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/01.STR.0000199147.30016.74</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nater</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bogousslavsky</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Regli</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stroke patterns with atrial septal aneurysm</article-title><source>Cererovascular Dis</source><year>1992</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>342</fpage><lpage>345</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1159/000109041</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Serva</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Catala</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Rancurel</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Posterior cerebral artery infarction: a study of 76 cases</article-title><source>Cerebrovascular disease</source><year>1992</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>233</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amarenco</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hauw</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cerebellar infarcts in the territory of the superior cerebellar artery; a clinicopathological study of 33 cases</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>1990</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>1383</fpage><lpage>1390</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2392223</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmahmann</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherman</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The cerebellar cognitive affective syndrome</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>1998</year><volume>121</volume><fpage>561</fpage><lpage>579</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9577385</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/brain/121.4.561</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Warlow</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Dennis</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Gijn</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Hankey</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandercock</surname><given-names>PAG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bamford</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wardlaw</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stroke: A practical guide to management</article-title><source>Where is the lesion?</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Blackwell science limited</publisher-name><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>124</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amarenco</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cerebellar infarctions and their mechanisms</article-title><source>Rev Neurol (Paris)</source><year>1993</year><volume>149</volume><fpage>728</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8091085</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carrera</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Michel</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bogousslavsky</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anteromedian, central and posterolateral infarcts of thalamus: three variant types</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>2004</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>2826</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15514194</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/01.STR.0000147039.49252.2f</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Warlow</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Dennis</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Gijn</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Hankey</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandercock</surname><given-names>PAG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bamford</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wardlaw</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stroke: A practical guide to management</article-title><source>What pathological type of stroke is it?</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Blackwell science limited</publisher-name><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>162</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>